🔹 What is Data Modeling?
Data modeling is the process of designing how data is structured, stored, and related to support business processes, analytics, and performance.
Goal: accuracy, scalability, performance, and usability.

🔹 Best Data Modeling Techniques
Dimensional Modeling (Star Schema)
Structure
Fact table → measures (sales, transactions)
Dimension tables → descriptive attributes

Snowflake Schema (Normalized Dimensions)
A variation of star schema where dimension tables are normalized into sub-dimensions.
✔ Example
Customer → City → State → Country
✔ Pros
✔ reduces redundancy
✔ improves data integrity
❌ Cons
❌ more joins → slower queries
Use when dimension hierarchies are complex.
